// Password Spraying, Many Accounts from One Source
// Detects password spraying: a burst of bad-password failures (Event ID 4625, SubStatus 0xC000006A) across many distinct accounts from one source in a short window. Spraying is defined by breadth, not depth. Requires an aggregation-capable backend; the condition expresses the intent (count distinct targets per source).
// techniques: T1110.003   severity: high   status: stable
// validate: Atomic Red Team T1110.003
//   Spray one password across 20+ accounts from a single host, e.g.
//   kerbrute passwordspray -d <domain> users.txt 'Autumn2026!'
// source: rules/credential-access/password-spraying-4625.yml  (GENERATED, do not edit by hand)
SecurityEvent
| where ((EventID =~ "4625") and (SubStatus =~ "0xc000006a"))
| summarize Hits=dcount(TargetUserName) by bin(TimeGenerated, 5m), IpAddress
| where Hits > 10
